      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              FABRIC CONSTRUCTION METHODS                         |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  WEAVING               KNITTING            FELTING              |\n|  =======               ========            =======              |\n|  Two yarn systems      One yarn system      No yarn system       |\n|  interlaced at 90°     looped into chains  Fibers entangled     |\n|                                            mechanically         |\n|  Warp + weft           Weft knitting:      Wet felting          |\n|                          horizontal loops   Needle felting       |\n|  Dimensionally stable  Warp knitting:                           |\n|  (no inherent stretch)   vertical chains   Cut without fraying  |\n|                                            Limited elasticity   |\n|  Frays when cut        Ladders when cut    Excellent insulation |\n|  Must be hemmed        (weft knitting)                          |\n|                                                                  |\n|  NONWOVENS             (a 4th method — no yarn, no interlacing) |\n|  =========             Fibers bonded: thermally, chemically,    |\n|                        mechanically, or hydroentangled          |\n|                        Disposables: diapers, masks, wipes       |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
