      },
      "text": "```\nWARP: yarns running lengthwise (parallel to selvage)\nWEFT: yarns interlacing crosswise (perpendicular to warp)\n      Also called: \"filling\" in industrial terminology"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:textiles:05-fabric-construction, git-history:textiles:05-fabric-construction]",
        "canonical_path": "textiles/05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md",
        "concepts": "[fabric, construction]",
        "current_path": "textiles/05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:textiles:fabric-construction",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "textiles",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[fabric, construction]",
        "section": "textiles",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fabric Construction",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LOOM ANATOMY:\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  BEAM (warp beam)                                        │\n  │  Wound with warp threads at back of loom                 │\n  │  Feeds warp under tension toward cloth beam              │\n  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │  HEDDLES + HARNESSES                                      │\n  │  Each warp thread passes through eye of a heddle         │\n  │  Heddles grouped in harnesses (frames)                   │\n  │  Harnesses rise/fall to create SHED                      │\n  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │  SHED: the opening between raised and lowered warp       │\n  │  Shuttle (or rapier/air jet) passes weft through shed    │\n  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │  REED (beater): comb that beats weft into previous picks │\n  │  Also spaces warp threads evenly                         │\n  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │  CLOTH BEAM: takes up woven fabric as it is produced     │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md#010",
      "path": [
        "05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:textiles:05-fabric-construction, git-history:textiles:05-fabric-construction]",
        "canonical_path": "textiles/05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md",
        "concepts": "[fabric, construction]",
        "current_path": "textiles/05-FABRIC-CONSTRUCTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:textiles:fabric-construction",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "textiles",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[fabric, construction]",
        "section": "textiles",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fabric Construction",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SEQUENCE (one weft pick):\n  1. Harnesses raise/lower → SHED opens\n  2. Shuttle/rapier passes weft through shed\n  3. REED beats weft into fell line (previous pick)\n  4. Harnesses change position → shed closes + opens new\n  5. Repeat\n```"
    },
