      "text": "```\nBACKSTRAP LOOM (~10,000 BCE, still used):\n  Warp: one end tied to fixed post, other end to weaver's waist\n  Body tension controls warp tension\n  Portable — used for fine ceremonial weaving in Andean/Southeast Asia\n  No machine — entire weave structure controlled by hand"
    },
    {
