      },
      "text": "WARP-WEIGHTED LOOM (ancient Greece/Scandinavia):\n  Warp threads hang vertically\n  Weights at bottom maintain tension\n  Woven from top down; shed stick and heddle rod for shed\n  Evidence from Greek vase paintings; archaeological weight finds"
    },
    {
